<%# The guide, the hub's main column, one step at a time (GuidePage). Its
    steps that act on the site sit where the participant does that thing:
    sign in first, Hackatime where the plugin goes in, the pet's project
    after Movement, and ship at the end. %>
<article class="guide panel" id="guide" data-controller="os-note">
  <header>
    <%# Shown only inside guide.txt's window, for reading it full size. %>
    <p class="guide-new-tab"><%= link_to "open the guide in a new tab ↗", request.path, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %></p>
    <h1>Build a desktop pet in Godot</h1>
    <% if @step == GuidePage.first %>
      <%# New text, in place of a placeholder. %>
      <p>You’ll build a little pet that lives on your desktop: a Godot game with no window frame and no background, just your sprite. It walks along your screen, turns around at the edges, stops for a rest now and then, and you can pick it up and drag it around.</p>
    <% end %>
    <%# The step that shows is marked in the list below, or in the outline
        beside the guide. A screen reader hears it here too. %>
    <p class="visually-hidden">step <%= @step.number %> of <%= GuidePage.all.size %>: <%= @step.name %></p>
  </header>

  <%# Every step, to go to any of them. Where the outline beside the guide
      lists the steps, this list hides. %>
  <nav class="guide-contents" aria-label="the guide's steps">
    <ol>
      <% GuidePage.all.each do |step| %>
        <li><%= link_to guide_page_path(step), aria: { current: ("page" if step == @step) }, data: { action: "guide-pager#go" } do %><span class="guide-contents-number"><%= step.number %></span> <%= step.name %><% end %></li>
      <% end %>
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <div class="guide-step">
    <%= render "guides/pages/#{@step.slug}" %>
  </div>
</article>
